    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.immediate_dominators - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.immediate_dominators.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.immediate_dominators()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find the immediate dominator of every node reachable from a start node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.immediate_dominators()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find the immediate dominator of every node reachable from a start node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.immediate_dominators()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Find the immediate dominator of every node reachable from a start node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind the immediate dominator of every node reachable from a start node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L66739-L66847){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.immediate_dominators(source)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Immediate dominators](../assets/graphs/immediate-dominators.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"An if/else control-flow graph: entry (outlined) leads to if, which branches to then and else; both rejoin at merge, which leads to exit. The dominator tree is drawn in the accent color: every path to merge passes through if but through neither branch, so the dashed accent arrow if to merge replaces the faded branch edges. The card maps each node to its immediate dominator: if for then, else and merge, merge for exit.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nIn a directed graph with a start node, a node `d` *dominates* node `v` if every path from\nthe start to `v` passes through `d`. The *immediate* dominator of `v` is its closest strict\ndominator, and linking every node to it forms the dominator tree. Dominators come from\ncompiler design (control-flow analysis, loop detection, placing code), and in networks\nthey identify single points of failure: a node's immediate dominator is the last\nunavoidable relay on the way from a source, such as a router every packet to a host must\ntraverse, or a gene that every regulatory path to another passes through.\n\nOnly nodes reachable from `source` appear in the result, and `source` maps to itself.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The start (entry) node, as an ID or label.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   For every reachable node ID, the ID of its immediate dominator.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected or `source` does not exist.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThis is the iterative algorithm of Cooper, Harvey and Kennedy (2001), as in NetworkX:\nnodes are processed in reverse postorder of a depth-first search, each node's dominator\nis updated to the nearest common dominator of its processed predecessors, and the pass\nrepeats until nothing changes. It is simple and fast in practice, $O(V^2)$ in the worst\ncase. Dominance frontiers follow from the dominator tree; see `dominance_frontiers()`.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~dominance_frontiers`) \n\n:   Where a node's dominance ends.\n\n[](`~ancestors`) \n\n:   Every node that can reach a node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nBoth branches of an if/else rejoin at `merge`, so the immediate dominator of `merge` is\n`if`, not either branch:\n\n::: {#6ebb75f5 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"entry\", \"if\"), (\"if\", \"then\"), (\"if\", \"else\"), (\"then\", \"merge\"),\n     (\"else\", \"merge\"), (\"merge\", \"exit\")],\n    directed=True,\n)\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\nboss = graph.immediate_dominators(\"entry\")\n\n{label(n): label(d) for n, d in boss.items()}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'entry': 'entry',\n 'if': 'entry',\n 'then': 'if',\n 'else': 'if',\n 'merge': 'if',\n 'exit': 'merge'}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Bottlenecks of a project\n\n`project()` is the plan for opening a made-up café, with an arrow from each task to every\ntask that can't start until it's done. A task's immediate dominator is the last task that\nevery path from the start to it goes through. Installing the equipment depends on two\nbranches, but both come out of the design:\n\n::: {#90cba51d .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncafe = ec.project()\nlabel = cafe.get_label_from_id\nboss = cafe.immediate_dominators(\"Start\")\n\n{label(n): label(d) for n, d in boss.items() if label(n) in\n [\"Install\", \"Training\", \"Soft opening\"]}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n{'Install': 'Design', 'Training': 'Sign lease', 'Soft opening': 'Sign lease'}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nJoining each task to its immediate dominator gives the dominator tree. Everything hangs\nfrom signing the lease, and the design governs its own branch of the plan:\n\n::: {#ef57469e .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntree = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(label(d), label(n)) for n, d in boss.items() if n != d],\n    directed=True,\n)\ntree.plot(label_by=\"label\", seed=2, height=420)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relat